            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for a resident, then the Bengali for to hang out (chatting)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: মাঠ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মাঠ — māṭh — \"a field; an open ground\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বিকেলে ছেলেরা মাঠে ফুটবল খেলে। bikele chhelerā māṭhe phuṭbôl khele. In the afternoons the boys play football on the field."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Open ground for games, meetings and grazing; a field of crops is a খেত."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "মাঠ (māṭh) is the open ground of every town and village; where the word comes from is not settled, and CDIAL gives no Bengali form for it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
