              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উঠোন — uṭhon — \"a courtyard (of a house)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "দিদিমা উঠোনে বসে চাল বাছছিলেন। didimā uṭhone bôse chāl bāchhchhilen. Grandmother sat in the courtyard picking over the rice."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The open yard in the middle of a village house, where work is done and children play."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "উঠোন (uṭhon) is inherited: CDIAL lists Bengali uṭhān, \"a courtyard\", under Sanskrit upasthā́na, \"approach, attendance\" and later \"an abode\" (CDIAL 2275); উঠোন is the everyday spoken form."
            }
          ]
